    "slug": "somali-president-says-ethiopia-can-access-sea-under-formal-agreement",
    "summary": "President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud stated Somalia is open to granting Ethiopia sea access for trade and economic purposes, provided it is done through a formal bilateral agreement that respects Somalia's sovereignty.",
    "content": "Somali President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud has stated that Somalia will not obstruct Ethiopia from obtaining sea access for its trade and economic needs, but emphasized that such an arrangement must be formalized through an official agreement between the two nations. In an interview with Al Jazeera, the president described relations between Somalia and Ethiopia as currently positive.\n\nPresident Mohamud said Somalia is willing to offer Ethiopia opportunities to use Somali maritime routes, provided that Somalia's independence, unity, and territorial integrity are respected. This marks a notable shift from previous tensions over the issue.\n\nThe statement follows a period of strained relations between the two neighbors after Ethiopia signed a memorandum of understanding with the self-declared republic of Somaliland in January 2024, which Somalia condemned as a violation of its sovereignty. The dispute had raised regional concerns and led to diplomatic efforts to de-escalate tensions.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant as it could affect regional stability, trade routes, and the political landscape in the Horn of Africa. Many in the diaspora maintain close ties to both Somalia and Ethiopia and have followed the dispute with concern, particularly regarding its potential impact on Somali sovereignty and regional cooperation.\n\nThe president's remarks suggest a possible path forward, but key details remain unclear, including the terms of any future agreement and whether Ethiopia will engage in direct talks with the Somali federal government. Observers note that any deal would need to balance Ethiopia's economic interests with Somalia's territorial integrity.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/04/madaxweyne-xasan-sheekh-soomaaliya-kama-hor-istaagayso-itoobiya-inay-hesho-marin-badeed/",
